{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115934-2e-suitable-banes","id":1115934,"title":"[2E] Suitable Banes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-14T07:09:36-07:00","id":1115934,"title":"[2E] Suitable Banes","content":"I create elder vampire - Deava (Arch)Bishop to be precise - and I look for good Individual Banes for Kindred. It's open call to all Clans and Covenants characters, as I plan to run some other vampire NPC.<br /> <br /> I very like example of 2E Bane mechanics with classical showing the Cross to vampire and him being hit with Bashing damage by it. Still, it does not sound as good Bane for Bishop living under literal mortal church cathedral catacombs. So I hope to get's some of your ideas on many vampires Banes, best sorted by Clan or Covenant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T21:23:50-07:00","id":1117085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1115934-2e-suitable-banes#post1115934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I create elder vampire - Deava (Arch)Bishop to be precise - and I look for good Individual Banes for Kindred. It's open call to all Clans and Covenants characters, as I plan to run some other vampire NPC.<br /> <br /> I very like example of 2E Bane mechanics with classical showing the Cross to vampire and him being hit with Bashing damage by it. Still, it does not sound as good Bane for Bishop living under literal mortal church cathedral catacombs. So I hope to get's some of your ideas on many vampires Banes, best sorted by Clan or Covenant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my Frailty Chronicle I have Personal Banes be the result of gaining Permanent Atrocity, basically having done grievous harm to others accumulate Temporary Atrocity until it converts to a Permanent Atrocity. The Bane they gain is related to the tipping point transgression, crossing running water for drowning someone or using a river to conceal the corpse, cold iron for using archaic iron torture implements to extract information, fire for burning a family alive in a building (I know vampires already have the bane of fire but I apply the Atrocity/Personal Bane system to all template beings), red headed women because that was the category of victim of the monster's horrible violation, ect...<br /> <br /> Basically I link it to horrible events the character did, making them a form of poetic or ironic justice/punishment.<br /> <br /> I'd make a laundry list of atrocities this bishop would have likely done, pick a few fill in some details and then have that be the seed the bane grew out of.<br /> <br /> That way you can research the horrors of the beings past to get hints as to what it's weaknesses may be, and is very flavorful way to use the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-17-2017, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}